   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening the Resilience of Rural Communities in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">to improve food security and nutrition governance and crises preparedness through evidence-based policymaking, early warning, strengthened institutional capacity, and orientation of strategic investments for food systems resilience. This Action contributes to SDG 2 ?end hunger, achieve food security and improved nutrition and promote sustainable agriculture?. The action is aligned and contributes to the three dimensions of the Global Network against food crisis: generation of evidence-based information and analysis, leveraging/ orienting decision making on strategic investments to prepare, prevent and respond to food crises, fostering political uptake and functional coordination across sectors addressing other dimensions driving food security crisis. Through evidence-based programming, the action will work alongside South Sudan national partners, including GRSS, UN agencies, NGOs and CBOs</narrative>
  </description>
